1nwj|n|A piggin. ; The young of swine, male or female; also, any swine; a hog. ; Any wild species of the genus Sus and related genera. ; An oblong mass of cast iron, lead, or other metal. See Mine pig, under Mine. ; One who is hoggish; a greedy person.	a:z2s,146,3~z2s,146,3	n:z2s,166,12~z2s,166,12
1nwk|n|Any bird of the order Columbae, of which numerous species occur in nearly all parts of the world. ; An unsuspected victim of sharpers; a gull.	v:1ngq,152,2~1ngq,152,2
