1o4y|n|A contagious disease of fowls, characterized by hoarseness, discharge from the nostrils and eyes, and an accumulation of mucus in the mouth, forming a "scale" on the tongue. By some the term pip is restricted to this last symptom, the disease being called roup by them. ; A seed, as of an apple or orange. ; One of the conventional figures or "spots" on playing cards, dominoes, etc.	n:1sov,68,2~1sov,68,2	N:gdv,83,1;15gl,58,7~15gl,58,7;gdv,83,1
